Use Case:
You want to process a large number of independent video transcoding jobs. Each job processes a video file to convert it to a different format. You want to use Spot Instances to reduce costs, and handle job retries automatically if interrupted.

Step 1: Create a Compute Environment
Defines the resources AWS Batch can use (EC2 Spot Instances with fallback to On-Demand).

bash
aws batch create-compute-environment \
  --compute-environment-name VideoTranscodeEnv \
  --type MANAGED \
  --state ENABLED \
  --compute-resources type=SPOT,minvCpus=0,maxvCpus=64,desiredvCpus=10,instanceTypes=c5.large,m5.large,spotIamFleetRole=arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/AmazonEC2SpotFleetRole,subnets=subnet-abc123,securityGroupIds=sg-0123456789abcdef0
---------------------------------------
Step 2: Create a Job Queue
Associates the compute environment to a logical queue where jobs wait to be scheduled.

bash
aws batch create-job-queue \
  --job-queue-name VideoTranscodeQueue \
  --state ENABLED \
  --priority 1 \
  --compute-environment-order order=1,computeEnvironment=VideoTranscodeEnv
-----------------------------------
Step 3: Register a Job Definition
Specifies the container image, resource requirements, retry strategy, and parameters.

Example JSON snippet:

json
{
  "jobDefinitionName": "video-transcode-job",
  "type": "container",
  "containerProperties": {
    "image": "123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/video-transcoder:latest",
    "vcpus": 2,
    "memory": 4096,
    "command": ["sh", "-c", "ffmpeg -i s3://my-input-bucket/input.mp4 -c:v libx264 s3://my-output-bucket/output.mp4"],
    "jobRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/AWSBatchJobRole"
  },
  "retryStrategy": {
    "attempts": 3
  }
}
Register with AWS CLI:

bash
aws batch register-job-definition --cli-input-json file://job-definition.json
-----------------------------------------
Step 4: Submit a Batch Job
bash
aws batch submit-job \
  --job-name video-transcode-job-1 \
  --job-queue VideoTranscodeQueue \
  --job-definition video-transcode-job
You can submit multiple jobs for many input files.

--------------------------------------------
Step 5: Monitor Job Status
bash
aws batch describe-jobs --jobs <jobId>
Or monitor via AWS console CloudWatch Logs.

Real-World Benefits:
Cost savings: Spot Instances reduce costs up to 90%.

Scalability: Automatically scale based on job load.

Fault tolerance: Retries jobs on failure or interruption.

Integration: Works seamlessly with S3, Lambda, SNS, and other AWS services.

Summary
AWS Batch abstracts the complexities of managing batch compute resource provisioning, scheduling, and scaling. It simplifies running large-scale batch jobs such as video transcoding, big data processing, and scientific simulations in a cost-effective, scalable manner.
